Python Advanced Built-in Functions

Write smarter, cleaner, and more Pythonic code

If you already know print() and len(), these are the next-level built-ins you must master 👇

⚙️ Functional Power
map() → Apply a function to every item
filter() → Select items based on condition
lambda → Anonymous one-line functions

👉 Used heavily in data processing & pipelines

🧠 Iteration & Control
enumerate() → Index + value (clean loops)
zip() → Combine multiple iterables
reversed() → Reverse iteration
sorted(key=…) → Custom sorting logic

✅ Logic & Validation
any() → True if any condition matches
all() → True if all conditions match
isinstance() → Safe type checking

👉 Cleaner than long if chains

🔍 Introspection & Debugging
dir() → Explore object attributes
vars() → Object’s __dict__
callable() → Check if object is callable
help() → Built-in documentation

🧩 Dynamic Execution (Use Carefully ⚠️)
eval() → Evaluate expressions
exec() → Execute dynamic code
compile() → Compile source into bytecode

👉 Powerful, but avoid in production unless necessary

🚀 Performance & Memory
iter() → Create iterators manually
next() → Fetch next value
slice() → Advanced slicing logic

💡 Why These Matter?
✔ Cleaner code
 ✔ Fewer loops
 ✔ More readable logic
 ✔ Strong interview signal
 ✔ Pythonic mindset
